    "knowledge_point": "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description",
    "problem": "Which of the following is a $2\\times 2$ matrix?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "- The matrix $P$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $Q$ has $4$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $R$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices.",
